"accessibility.repairInstructions" = "After an update or a change in app signing, macOS may retain an old permission entry. Repair will clear cpsmart’s old entry, open the correct System Settings page, and then quit the app.\n\nAfter the app quits:\n\n1. Click “+” below the list.\n2. Select /Applications/cpsmart.app and turn on its switch.\n3. Relaunch cpsmart from Applications.\n\nmacOS requires you to turn on the final permission switch yourself.";
"update.installationInstructions" = "{0}\n\nTo finish installing:\n1. Click “Quit cpsmart” below.\n2. Drag the new version from the disk image to Applications, then choose “Replace”.\n3. Relaunch cpsmart.\n\nIf automatic pasting stops working after the update, try pasting once more and choose the permission repair option. cpsmart will clear its old permission entry, open the correct settings page, and quit. Then click “+”, add /Applications/cpsmart.app, enable its switch, and relaunch the app.";
